			"notes": "# Blurpstone v1.1.0\n\nDiscord bridge polish: configurable prefix colors, role-colored names, and safe ping handling.\n\n---\n\n## New Features\n\n### Customizable `[Discord]` prefix colors\n\nThe prefix shown for messages relayed from Discord to Minecraft is now fully themeable via three independent config keys:\n\n| Key | Controls | Default |\n|-----|----------|---------|\n| `bracketsColor` | The `[` and `]` characters | `#5865F2` |\n| `discordTextColor` | The word **Discord** | `#FFFFFF` |\n| `contentColor` | Message body + author fallback | `#FFFFFF` |\n\nAll keys accept a hex string (with or without `#`). Invalid values fall back to the defaults above.\n\n### Discord role colors in-game\n\nWhen a message is bridged from Discord, the author's name is now rendered in the color of their **highest-positioned colored role** — matching what Discord users see in the server member list. Members without any colored role fall back to `contentColor`.\n\n### Mention sanitization (Minecraft → Discord)\n\nWebhooks bypass Discord's \"Mention Everyone\" permission, which meant a Minecraft player typing `@everyone` would ping the entire Discord server. This release neutralizes all pings before sending:\n\n- `@everyone` → `@​everyone` (zero-width space; text stays readable, no ping)\n- `@here` → `@​here`\n- `<@id>`, `<@!id>`, `<@&id>`, `<#id>` are stripped entirely\n\n---\n\n## Configuration\n\nThe `config/blurpstone.json` file gains three new fields. Existing configs continue to work — missing keys are filled with defaults on next load:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"botToken\": \"YOUR_BOT_TOKEN\",\n  \"guildId\": \"YOUR_SERVER_ID\",\n  \"channelId\": \"YOUR_CHANNEL_ID\",\n  \"discordOwnerUserId\": \"YOUR_DISCORD_USER_ID\",\n  \"bracketsColor\": \"#5865F2\",\n  \"discordTextColor\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n  \"contentColor\": \"#FFFFFF\"\n}"
		},
